            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025:F026\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) establishes the general railroad crossing stopping requirement while explicitly carving out paragraph (b) ('Except as provided in paragraph (b) of this section'). Paragraph (b)(1) provides that a stop need not be made at a streetcar crossing or industrial switching tracks within a business district. Setting an explicit exception edge from C0009 targeting C0000 faithfully models this qualification.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025\", \"F027\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) mandates stopping prior to crossing railroad tracks at grade except as provided in paragraph (b). Paragraph (b)(2) exempts the driver from stopping when a police officer or crossing flagman directs traffic to proceed. Adding an explicit exception qualification link from C0010 to baseline claim C0000 accurately reflects this statutory caveat.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025\", \"F028\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) conditions its railroad crossing stopping requirement on paragraph (b), and paragraph (b)(3) exempts crossings controlled by a functioning green traffic signal permitting transit without stopping under local law. Qualifying baseline C0000 with C0011 via an exception relation correctly implements this explicit caveat.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0003\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025\", \"F029\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) creates the baseline duty to stop before crossing tracks at grade subject to paragraph (b), and paragraph (b)(4) specifies that a stop need not be made at marked abandoned crossings. Establishing an exception edge from 